**Definition 8.2 (primary mathematical precedents).** The new content here
is the repository-derived unary/74-role/raw-control instance, joint
retention join and exact current-owner source family. The intermediate
port, simulation, replay and factorization ideas have the following
precedents; no literature originality claim is made.

Maignan and Spicher, *Causal Graph Dynamics and Kan Extensions*,
[primary text, §1.2](https://arxiv.org/html/2403.13393v6), define an edge
as a nonintersecting pair of vertex/port endpoints: a port occurs in at
most one edge. This allows an empty child port and hence unary storage;
it does not require full binary branching. Their synchronous-union and
renaming results are not an initialization, authority or tariff theorem
for this rooted sequential primitive. Endpoint consistency and the
initialized row square are established here by the explicit templates.

Lynch and Vaandrager, *Forward and Backward Simulations—Part I: Untimed
Systems*, [author abstract](https://groups.csail.mit.edu/tds/papers/Lynch/IC95.html),
distinguish refinements, simulations and history/prophecy relations.
The row square here is proved directly, retaining each actual native
cut; a trace-level simulation alone would not establish these cuts,
current owner rights or their prices.

Bennett, *Logical Reversibility of Computation*,
[primary text](https://www.cs.princeton.edu/courses/archive/fall06/cos576/papers/bennett73.html),
uses explicitly retained history and additional computation to manage
information discarded by overwriting. Here the consumed inputs and
finite stopping ordinal permit forward reconstruction on an actual
image; neither reversible physical evolution, free uncomputation nor
a thermodynamic inference is used.

